meta {
  name: Subscription - Cancellation Options
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/subscription/cancellation
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

docs {
  Everything the cancellation screens need: the reasons to choose from, the
  one offer (if any) that goes with each, and the date the plan would end.
  Requires the `billing.manage` permission. Returns `404` when the workspace
  has no subscription.

  `offer` is `null` or `{ type, percent_off, months }`, where `type` is:

  - `discount`: `percent_off` for `months` monthly invoices. Only for the
    `too_expensive` reason, on a monthly subscription, once per workspace
    per `BILLING_CANCELLATION_OFFER_COOLDOWN_MONTHS`. Never offered when
    `BILLING_CANCELLATION_DISCOUNT_PERCENT` is 0.
  - `downgrade`: a cheaper paid plan is on sale; send the customer to the
    plans screen.
  - `help`: the customer can ask for help instead of cancelling.

  No offer is made to a subscription that is on trial, failing payment, or
  already scheduled to end.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { ends_at, reasons: [{ value, label, comment_prompt, offer }] } }`.
}
